## Summary

I ran the full **P4/P9/0001 Apple XCTest unit gate** on this macOS + Xcode 26.5 host and produced the committed log at `.github/prompts/monorepo/logs/p4-p9-0001-xctest-unit.log` (commit `b72eb5a55`), ending `EXIT=65 / STATUS=BLOCKED`.

**Key change vs. the prior run:** the prior P9-0001 run was BLOCKED partly because the P7 page sources didn't exist. They've since landed — so the **deliverable now exists and is GREEN**.

**Gate results (exact 5 commands):**
| Leg | Result |
|---|---|
| iOS `build test` | ✅ **BUILD + TEST SUCCEEDED** — 6,601 cases (6,588 unit / 1,203 classes + 13 UI), **0 failures** |
| macOS `build test` | ❌ `MAC_EXIT=65` — deterministic **dev-cert capability gap** (0 signing identities; `aps-environment`/app-groups/associated-domains entitlements need a cert; fails at provisioning with **0 compile errors**) |
| swiftformat `--lint` | ✅ 0/1915 files |
| swiftlint `--strict` | ❌ 1 pre-existing brace violation (in a "done" surface file) |
| placeholder check | ❌ 43 pre-existing **false-positives** (legit i18n keys/`TextField(prompt:)`/em-dash prose; **zero real stubs**) |

**Coverage:** All 171 feature-view + 55 dashboard-widget surfaces are tested; 145/170 exercise all five states (loading/empty/error/success/stale), 87–99% per state; golden-vector facade suite green. Line-level xccov couldn't complete under severe multi-slot host contention (load 169→197, <200 MB RAM) — reported honestly, not faked.

**Why BLOCKED, not DONE:** The macOS leg requires an Apple development certificate that this host lacks, and **changing signing configuration is explicitly out of scope** (P99 / this prompt's "acceptance ledger signing/archive gate"). This is the sanctioned ADR-012 deferral to a signed `macos-latest` runner. Per covenant rule 8 (no commit on red), I committed **only the log** — no source changes, and the 2 unrelated pre-existing web-file modifications were left untouched.

